            },
            "body": "The `johnbillion/wp-compat` PHPStan extension that now ships with `wp-cli-tests` reported 28 errors. It checks every WordPress symbol against the WordPress 4.9 baseline that `wp-cli-tests` configures, and only recognizes `function_exists()` and `method_exists()` guards, so it cannot see the per-command `before_invoke` checks in `block-command.php`.\n\nAll 28 are false positives, and this package made that unusually easy to verify: it already gates each subcommand on its own version, so every finding can be checked against the gate of the command that actually contains it. Every symbol sits at or below its gate.\n\n| Command | Gate | Symbols flagged | Version |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `wp block type` | 5.0 | `WP_Block_Type_Registry::get_instance()`, `::get_all_registered()`, `::get_registered()`, `::is_registered()`, `WP_Block_Type::is_dynamic()` | 5.0.0 |\n| `wp block synced-pattern` | 5.0 | `parse_blocks()` | 5.0.0 |\n| `wp block style` | 5.3 | `WP_Block_Styles_Registry::get_instance()`, `::get_all_registered()`, `::get_registered_styles_for_block()` | 5.3.0 |\n| `wp block pattern` | 5.5 | `WP_Block_Patterns_Registry::get_instance()`, `::get_all_registered()`, `::get_registered()` | 5.5.0 |\n| `wp block pattern-category` | 5.5 | `WP_Block_Pattern_Categories_Registry::get_instance()`, `::get_all_registered()`, `::get_registered()` | 5.5.0 |\n| `wp block template` | 5.9 | `get_block_template()`, `get_block_templates()` | 5.8.0 |\n| `wp block binding` | 6.5 | `get_block_bindings_source()`, `get_all_registered_block_bindings_sources()` | 6.5.0 |\n\nIgnored per file, matching on the message as well as the identifier so each entry pins the version its command is gated on. That matters here more than anywhere: with seven different gates, a file-wide `WPCompat.methodNotAvailable` ignore would let a symbol newer than any given command's gate pass unnoticed. Pinned this way, such a call still gets reported.\n\nNo source changes: nothing here is an actual compatibility problem.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun locally against the same dependency versions CI resolves (`johnbillion/wp-compat` 2.0.0, `php-stubs/wordpress-stubs` v6.9.4, `wp-cli/wp-cli-tests` v5.2.3):\n\n- `composer phpstan` — `[OK] No errors`, with no unmatched ignore entries\n- As a control, adding a deliberately dead ignore entry does produce an `ignore.unmatched` error, confirming the entries above match real errors rather than sitting there unused\n\nGitHub Actions was failing to allocate runners across the org while this was written, so CI may need a re-run once that clears.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSjnuDoRgWkj4DjRgHbtNB)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated static analysis configuration to account for supported WordPress block APIs across multiple WordPress versions.\n  * Reduced false-positive compatibility warnings for block-related commands.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
